== Accepted scope and inference
Let p > max(3,s), even s ≥ 2, with nonzero original weights in two disjoint s-bit affine abscissa maps. Retain the nonsingular short Weierstrass curve and finite rational target R=(r,t), t ≠ 0. F0 lists its 2s Boolean equations and raw fixed-target S3. Fg groups pairs within each coordinate, uses three indicators for the nonzero words, lists their Boolean and pairwise-product equations, and substitutes into raw S3. It has 3s variables and 6s local quadratics plus S3; no circuit auxiliaries or affine reduction.

For one pair, zero and the three unit vectors encode the four words. Projection b0=u10+u11, b1=u01+u11 has inverse u10=b0(1−b1), u01=(1−b0)b1, u11=b0b1. Exact bit models and affine quotient rings correspond. Ambient ideals are in different rings; coordinate injectivity is a separate premise.

$ d_("reg")(F_0) = 1 + (3s)/2, quad d_("reg")(F_g) = s+1 $
$ d_("reg")(F_0) - d_("reg")(F_g) = s/2 $

Degree here is the first component filled by the ideal of the *listed generators' highest homogeneous parts* [1]. The source-qualified mutant-closure corollary is sd_sigma(Fg) ≤ max(s+2,4)=s+2 [3]. The raw quartic input still matters at s=2. This gives no strict ordering of actual solving degrees.

