== Comparison with the frozen producer
The local top quotient is a tensor product of s factors k⊕k³ with square-zero positive part, giving Hilbert series (1+3T)^s. Its top degree survives after quotienting each factor by the corresponding coordinate contribution, which kills the raw quartic top. Together with the local bound this proves the exact grouped value. The original threshold follows separately from weighted blockwise Lefschetz at p>s, with exact ranks and a nonzero preceding-degree component [2].

