The general local construction over any field gives H(T)=∏g(1+(2^w_g−1)T), exact local threshold G+1, and only an upper bound for arbitrary added equations. The seven false-control classes are addressed: missing pairwise products; missing zero word; unanalyzed auxiliaries; missing characteristic/weight premises; constant one; growing width; and unqualified matrix/runtime transfer. For example, adjoining z=u² to u²−u leaves highest-part ideal (u²) in k[u,z], so graded finiteness need not survive a reconstructible auxiliary.

Both reviews additionally derive odd-width and locally reduced-list results, including a separate s=2 proof. Their common formula 2 ceil(s/2)+1 is retained as a *reviewer-derived extension outside this decision's accepted frozen producer scope*. No broader acceptance or promotion is inferred.

